<title>SINGAPORE: British Petroleum gets 400,000 bbls more Nov LSWR.</title>
<headline>British Petroleum gets 400,000 bbls more Nov LSWR.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's state oil company, Pertamina has allocated an additional 400,000 barrels of November low sulphur waxy residue (LSWR) to British Petroleum, industry sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Earlier, BP had already been allocated a total of 1.12 million barrels of LSWR out of Pertamina's November allocation of 3.6 million barrels.</p>
<p>The additional allocation would bring BP's total allocation to 1.52 million barrels for lifting in November, sources said.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-870-3082)</p>
</text>
